course: dictionary
lesson: 16024
title: The word vendor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A vendor is a person or company that sells something. «The ice-cream vendor rang his bell at the park gate.» The clue is the word sells in the sentence: the vendor is the one selling the ice cream, not the one buying it.
explain: A street vendor sells food or goods outside, in the street or at a market stall. «A street vendor sold hot corn on the corner.» Ask yourself: who is selling the hot corn? That is the vendor.
explain: Vendor can also mean the person selling a house. «The vendor agreed to sell the house to the young family.» In this sentence the vendor is the seller, and the young family are the buyers.
fact: A vendor is a person or company that sells something.
fact: A street vendor sells food or goods in the street.
fact: In a house sale, the vendor is the person selling the house.
fact: Vendor is a noun, and its plural is vendors.
fact: The opposite of a vendor is a buyer, the person who buys.
exercise: «The ice-cream vendor rang his bell at the park gate.» What is a vendor? | A child who likes ice cream | A bell that rings loudly | *Someone who sells things | Someone who buys things at the park
exercise: «A street vendor sold hot corn on the corner.» Who sold the hot corn? | *The street vendor | The hungry children | The buyer with a coin | The corner
exercise: «The vendor agreed to sell the house to the young family.» Who is selling the house? | The buyer | The house | *The vendor | The young family
test: «The buyer paid the vendor for the bike.» Who gets the money? | The bike | The shop door | The buyer | *The vendor
test: Which word is the plural of vendor? | *vendors | vendori | vendor's | vendoring
exam: Which sentence uses vendor correctly? | Vendor is a loud bell that rings at the park | The vendor was very tall and green | The vendor ran across the road quickly | *The street vendor sold roasted nuts on the corner
